<title>UK: BOE says money market shortage taken out.</title>
<headline>BOE says money market shortage taken out.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said the residual shortage in the money market was zero after it revised the liquidity shortage to 1.25 billion stg from 1.4 billion at the previous estimate.</p>
<p>It said no use so far has been made of the discount houses late repo facility. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
